    <item>
      <title>1.0.3</title>
      <pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>103</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0.3</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <link>https://github.com/broodingjay/dispatch-releases/releases/tag/v1.0.3</link>
      <description><![CDATA[
        <h3>Fixes</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Keyboard Shortcuts is in the action bar again.</strong> In 1.0.2 the entry
              was registered only while a piece was open, so searching &#8984;K for it from the
              library &#8212; the one place the <strong>?</strong> button lives &#8212; answered
              &#8220;No matching actions&#8221;.</li>
        </ul>
      ]]></description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/broodingjay/dispatch-releases/releases/download/v1.0.3/Dispatch.dmg" sparkle:edSignature="HL3bzUa/E1r0QIeYuJweyhjc8KVlzo33vOUa/QIpmDmbsI/uaGIu9ncwG5EipOknitSUSrF99L6mLP4mVpctAA==" length="3712707" type="application/octet-stream"></enclosure>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>1.0.2</title>
      <pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>102</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0.2</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <link>https://github.com/broodingjay/dispatch-releases/releases/tag/v1.0.2</link>
      <description><![CDATA[
        <h3>Using the same writing on a second Mac</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Settings &#8594; Library &#8594; Use Existing Folder&#8230;</strong> points
              Dispatch at writing that is already on disk &#8212; a Dropbox or iCloud folder that
              synced down to another Mac before Dispatch was installed there. Nothing is copied,
              moved or deleted on either side.</li>
          <li>Previously the only option was <strong>Move&#8230;</strong>, which refuses a folder
              that already has files in it, so a second machine could not be set up at all.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Keyboard</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>A <strong>?</strong> in the bottom-left corner of the library lists every key
              Dispatch listens for.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Fixes</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>An externally-opened file no longer loses its frontmatter after switching apps.</li>
          <li><strong>Save a Copy of Everything</strong> twice in the same minute no longer
              deletes the first backup.</li>
          <li>Licence checks no longer follow a redirect away from the store.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Update channel</h3>
        <p><strong>Updates work again.</strong> Every build so far required a signed update feed
           and the published feed was not signed, so no copy would ever have accepted an update.
           If you are reading this in the updater, that is the fix working.</p>
      ]]></description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/broodingjay/dispatch-releases/releases/download/v1.0.2/Dispatch.dmg" sparkle:edSignature="jo1e18NZq8EUUo4jSXByQw9gbjd5ltdk1k/EZMUQvQxkD4J5uuHt09WxxYu07tcn/ZCfwPK3/HmI9LCu1us6Bw==" length="3712970" type="application/octet-stream"></enclosure>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>1.0.1</title>
      <pubDate>Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>101</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <link>https://github.com/broodingjay/dispatch-releases/releases/tag/v1.0.1</link>
      <description><![CDATA[
        <h3>Opening files that aren&#8217;t in your library</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Dispatch opens <code>.md</code>, <code>.markdown</code> and <code>.txt</code>
              files from anywhere. Double-click one in Finder, use Open With, or drag it onto
              the Dispatch icon in the Dock. Edits save back to the file where it is.</li>
          <li>To make Dispatch the default for a file type: Finder &#8594; Get Info &#8594;
              Open With &#8594; Change All. In 1.0 this appeared to work and then did nothing.</li>
          <li>Tags, goals, status and starring are turned off for a file outside your library.
              Those are stored in the file itself, and Dispatch does not add them to a file it
              did not create.</li>
          <li>A file that already has its own frontmatter is shown and saved whole, exactly as
              written.</li>
          <li>Opening several files at once shows the first. Any that aren&#8217;t shown are
              named on screen rather than dropped silently.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Known:</strong> opening a file when Dispatch isn&#8217;t already running
           leaves a second, empty window behind the document.</p>
      ]]></description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/broodingjay/dispatch-releases/releases/download/v1.0.1/Dispatch.dmg" sparkle:edSignature="HdwRfS5thWNTCXyPL+WCh0h4Rla9gZQptBDbSMxPbKQs+zM5tNhUbasng94MB09Vp+KcC7eKMsbSLjJRjNn0CQ==" length="3636714" type="application/octet-stream"></enclosure>
    </item>
